WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.853
I was seventeen when I found my first summer job, in a café by the sea in Brittany. I had to serve customers on the terrace from eleven to seven, six days a week. I thought it would be easy. I was wrong.

00:00:15.103 --> 00:00:34.533
On the first day, the weather was lovely and the terrace was full. I was running between the tables with trays that were too heavy, forgetting orders and mixing up white coffees with hot chocolates. Around three o'clock, I dropped a whole tray in front of a family of six. The silence that followed lasted an eternity.

00:00:34.783 --> 00:00:52.349
I was sure the boss was going to fire me. Instead, he brought me a broom, helped me pick everything up and said: 'Everyone breaks a tray one day. What matters is not breaking two.' Then he showed me how to carry a tray with one hand, close to the body.

00:00:52.599 --> 00:01:04.085
I worked in that café for three summers. I never broke another tray, and above all I learned something I have not forgotten: we learn better when someone gives us the right to make mistakes.
